module Collections

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Creates an empty split list. Heap-allocates the entity with every column null (`hijacked_none`) and
### the counts zero via the `hollow[T]()` footprint-alloc primitive; the first `add_last` reserves the
### backing column buffers.
### :returns: An empty `SplitList[T]`.
@rf("SplitList")
routine SplitList[T]() -> SplitList[T]
